            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Enhanced Vegetation Index",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Data inputs included 0.05\u00b0 16-day Enhanced Vegetation Index (EVI) and NDVI data products from MODIS (MOD13C1v006) downloaded from the date closest to the 15th of each month for 2000-201658.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MODIS",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "normalized difference vegetation index",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Existing continental and global upscaled products, including the FLUXCOM31 and FluxSat 32 products, were designed for continental-scale and global analysis and are generally based on remotely sensed estimates of photosynthetically active vegetation, such as the fraction of absorbed photosynthetically active radia- tion (fAPAR) and vegetation indices like the normalized differ- ence vegetation index (NDVI).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MODIS",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "gross primary productivity",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "The global Moderate Resolution Imaging Spectroradiometer (MODIS) GPP products are based on satellite data and include biome-specific light use efficiency values and atmospheric demand scalars, but still rely heavily on mea- sures of satellite greenness.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "MODIS",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MOUNTED_ON",
            "target_entity_instance": "Terra",
            "target_entity_type": "Platform",
            "paragraph": "Didan, K. MOD13C1 MODIS/Terra Vegetation Indices 16-Day L3 Global 0.05Deg CMG V006. NASA EOSDIS Land Processes DAAC. https:// doi.org/10.5067/MODIS/MOD13C1.006 (NASA EOSDIS Land Processes DAAC, 2015).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "DryFlux",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "R2",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The relation- ship between modeled (DryFlux) and observed (tower) monthly GPP for 2000-2015 with DryFlux had an R2 of 0.88 across all sites, compared to R2 = 0.43 for FLUXCOM and R2 = 0.41 for MODIS GPP (Fig. 1c).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "DryFlux",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "RMSE",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The model had a training accuracy of R2 = 0.815; RMSE = 0.521 with mtry = 10. The testing accuracy of the model was R2 = 0.610 and RMSE = 0.876.",
